{"id":"20260827T223402.646932578Z-06b45f7e","time":"2026-08-27T22:34:02.646932578Z","session_id":"session-20260827T222335.808640833Z","task_id":"task-1787869415809301617","source":"system","kind":"status","summary":"Authority for this plan, by lane.\n\nrequested objective:\n  gosumcheck's verbose output reports, for each remote fetch, the elapsed time and the target. Include the number of bytes received on that same line, with no change to non-verbose output or to any error path.\n  NOT established as a human objective — submitted unattended; no human presence was established\n  the wording is the task; it is not a person's authorization for it\n\ntechnical claims:\n  [evidence-bearing] Scoped Sensei preflight classifies the main.go change as LOW_RISK with local blast radius, no approval gate, and no anchored rule applying to the file. (gosumcheck/main.go) — source: graph\n  [evidence-bearing] clientOps.ReadRemote emits its verbose line only after a 200 response and a successful io.ReadAll; transport, status, and body-read errors return before that output. (gosumcheck/main.go:clientOps.ReadRemote) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The data returned by clientOps.ReadRemote is the successful io.ReadAll result, bounded by the existing 1 MiB LimitReader, so len(data) measures the body bytes delivered to gosumcheck rather than wire-level transfer size. (gosumcheck/main.go:clientOps.ReadRemote) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The ClientOps contract defines ReadRemote as returning remote content and requires errors for non-200 HTTP responses. (sumdb/client.go:ClientOps.ReadRemote) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] gosumcheck's init configures http.DefaultClient and clientOps.ReadRemote fetches through http.Get, providing the existing default-client transport seam for a network-free test. (gosumcheck/main.go:init and gosumcheck/main.go:clientOps.ReadRemote) — source: repository\n  [evidence-bearing] The gosumcheck directory currently has no Go test file; its existing test.bash builds the command and runs it with -v. (gosumcheck) — source: repository\n  the objective does not establish any of these. Evidence does.\n\nconsequence decision:\n  BOUNDED — the candidate worktree: files are edited in an isolated checkout, the diff is audited before it leaves, and discarding the worktree leaves the world unchanged\n  assessed from the action, not from who asked and not from whether the plan satisfies the objective.\n\nrouted: architectural-authority-granted\n"}
